# MARTA MATE Project Rule

You are building MARTA MATE, a privacy-conscious safety and well-being companion for late-night and nontraditional-hour transit riders in Atlanta.

Read AGENTS.md and docs/PRODUCT_CONTEXT.md before major work.

Prioritize a complete, polished, demoable journey over feature quantity:
Landing -> Login -> Plan Trip -> Virtual Buddies -> Match -> Calm Mode -> Safety Hub -> Arrival Check-In.

Use TypeScript, functional React components, clear interfaces, and modular components.

Use deterministic seed data and API fallbacks so the demo remains functional without keys or network access.

Do not introduce exact GPS tracking, public rider maps, real emergency dispatch, or real peer-to-peer chat.

Before adding a dependency, consider whether native browser APIs or existing packages can solve the problem.

Use accessible semantic markup, keyboard-friendly controls, labels, visible focus states, and mobile-first layout.
